# Set the default behavior, in case people don't have core.autocrlf set.
* text=auto
#* text eol=crlf
#* text eol=lf
#* text=off

*.dart text
*.txt text
*.dna text
*.py text

# Shell scripts must keep LF in the working tree even on Windows. Under the `* text=auto` rule
# above they would be checked out with CRLF, and bash then fails on the shebang
# ("/usr/bin/env: 'bash\r': No such file or directory") and never terminates heredocs. This
# matters for branch-for-issue.sh, which CONTRIBUTING.md tells Windows users to run in Git Bash,
# and for standalone/generate-icons.sh, which build-and-deploy.yml runs with `bash`.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf